<section aria-labelledby="size-h">
  <h2 id="size-h" class="type-h2">Size and color</h2>
  <p>The <code>icon</code> class sets the size to 20px by 20px, as a block that does not shrink. Inside a <a href="/components/button/">button</a> the icon is 8px from the label. Inside an icon-only button it sits in a 48px square. For color, set <code>color</code> on the parent, not on the icon.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="a11y-h">
  <h2 id="a11y-h" class="type-h2">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The <code>icon</code> shortcode adds <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> and <code>focusable="false"</code>, so an icon is skipped by screen readers.</li>
    <li>An icon alone never carries the meaning. An icon-only button needs an <code>aria-label</code>. An external link adds hidden text, "(opens in new tab)".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="add-h">
  <h2 id="add-h" class="type-h2">Adding an icon</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Take the SVG from the Outlined set of <code>@material-design-icons/svg</code>.</li>
    <li>Remove its <code>width</code> and <code>height</code> and set <code>fill="currentColor"</code>.</li>
    <li>Save it in <code>src/assets/icons/</code> with a lowercase name that uses underscores, such as <code>arrow_forward.svg</code>.</li>
    <li>Add its name to the list in <code>LICENSE.txt</code> in the same folder.</li>
    <li>Use it with <code>{% raw %}{% icon "arrow_forward" %}{% endraw %}</code>. The build stops with an error if the name does not match a file.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

